+    *   **Edges (2D) / Faces (3D):** For each edge (pair of pixels) or face (quad of voxels) in the neighborhood, let $I_{min}$ be the minimum intensity of its constituent vertices [S1, unofficial]. Decrement $H[I_{min}]$ by 1 [S1, unofficial]. This represents the edge/face entering the super level set when $T < I_{min}$ [S1, unofficial].
+    *   **Faces (2D) / Cells (3D):** For each face (quad of pixels) or cell (hexahedron of voxels) in the neighborhood, let $I_{min}$ be the minimum intensity of its constituent vertices [S1, unofficial]. Increment $H[I_{min}]$ by 1 [S1, unofficial]. This represents the face/cell entering the super level set when $T < I_{min}$ [S1, unofficial].
+    *   *Note:* In 3D, the pattern continues with the next Betti number, which is achieved by decrementing the histogram for 8-voxel-cubes in a $2 \times 2 \times 2$ neighborhood [S1, unofficial].
+4.  **Accumulate:** After the raster scan, compute the accumulated histogram $H_{acc}$ by summing $H$ from the highest bin downwards [S1, unofficial]:
     $$ H_{acc}[T] = \sum_{i=T}^{I_{max}} H[i] $$
     $H_{acc}[T]$ now contains the Euler Characteristic $\chi(T)$ of the super level set at isovalue $T$ [S1, unofficial].
